import PaymentProvider from '../components/PaymentProvider.astro';
---

<Marketing title="Terms" description="MCP Warp terms of service.">
  <section class="legal">
    <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="effective-date"><strong>Effective date:</strong> September 13, 2026</p>

    <div class="callout">
      <p><strong>The short version.</strong> This summary is for convenience only — the full Terms below are what applies.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>MCP Warp gives your local MCP servers a public, OAuth-protected URL. You're responsible for what your servers expose and for the account you keep it under.</li>
        <li>There's a <strong>Free</strong> plan (100 requests/month, 1 server) and paid <strong>Plus</strong> ($5/month) and <strong>Pro</strong> ($10/month) plans. Usage resets at the start of every UTC month.</li>
        <li>Paid plans are billed through our payment provider, which acts as merchant of record. Cancel anytime from Settings &gt; Billing via the billing portal, or by emailing <a href="mailto:support@mcpwarp.io">support@mcpwarp.io</a> — access continues until the end of the period you've paid for. There's a <strong>14-day money-back guarantee</strong> on your first payment.</li>
        <li>The tunnel relays your MCP traffic — it does not store request or response bodies.</li>
        <li>The Service is provided <strong>"as is"</strong>, best-effort, with no uptime guarantee.</li>
        <li>Our liability is limited: at most, what you paid us in the last 12 months.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <p>
      These Terms of Service ("Terms") govern your use of the mcpwarp.io website, the
      <code>mcpwarp</code> CLI, and the MCP Warp dashboard and tunnel service (collectively, the
      "Service"). The Service is operated by <a href="https://anatoly.dev">Anatoly Tarnavsky</a>,
      sole proprietor ("MCP Warp", "we", "us"). By accessing or using the Service, you agree to
      these Terms.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Acceptance of Terms</h2>
    <p>
      By using mcpwarp.io, the <code>mcpwarp</code> CLI, or the dashboard and tunnel service, you
      agree to be bound by these Terms. If you do not agree, do not use the Service.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Description of Service</h2>
    <p>MCP Warp is a tunnel service for the Model Context Protocol (MCP). The Service includes:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>The mcpwarp.io website (documentation and blog)</li>
      <li>The <code>mcpwarp</code> CLI, a Go binary distributed via Homebrew, Scoop, Linux packages, and GitHub</li>
      <li>The dashboard at <a href="https://web.mcpwarp.io">web.mcpwarp.io</a>, where you manage servers, tokens, and billing</li>
      <li>
        The tunnel infrastructure — a hosted relay that gives each MCP server you register a
        public, OAuth-protected URL at
        <code>https://&lt;name&gt;-&lt;username&gt;.tunnel.mcpwarp.io/mcp</code>, so that MCP
        clients such as Claude, ChatGPT, VS Code, and any Streamable HTTP MCP client can reach it
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. Account Registration and Eligibility</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Accounts are managed through our self-hosted Keycloak identity provider.</li>
      <li>You must be at least <strong>13 years old</strong> to create an account.</li>
      <li>Access to your servers is owner-only: there is no sharing and no anonymous access.</li>
      <li>You are responsible for keeping your account credentials and any personal access tokens (<code>mcpwarp_pat_...</code>) secure, and for all activity under your account.</li>
      <li>You must provide accurate information when creating your account and choosing your username, which forms part of every tunnel URL you're assigned.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>4. Your Responsibilities and Acceptable Use</h2>
    <p>You agree to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Use the Service in compliance with all applicable laws.</li>
      <li>Not use the Service to create, store, or relay illegal, harmful, or infringing content.</li>
      <li>Not attempt to disrupt, overload, probe, or reverse-engineer the tunnel infrastructure.</li>
      <li>
        Take responsibility for what your MCP servers expose. You choose which local servers to
        register and which MCP clients to authorize — we do not inspect or vouch for the content
        or behavior of either.
      </li>
      <li>
        Respect the terms of any third-party MCP client (Claude, ChatGPT, VS Code, or otherwise)
        you connect through the tunnel. We are not responsible for how those clients behave or
        handle data once a request reaches them.
      </li>
      <li>Observe fair use of the Pro plan's unlimited-server allowance — see "Subscription Tiers" below.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>5. Subscription Tiers</h2>
    <p>The Service currently offers three tiers:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Free:</strong> 100 requests/month, 1 server. No payment required.</li>
      <li><strong>Plus:</strong> unlimited requests, 1 server, for a recurring fee of $5/month.</li>
      <li><strong>Pro:</strong> unlimited requests, unlimited servers (subject to fair use), for a recurring fee of $10/month.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      The quota month is the UTC calendar month. Requests over your plan's quota receive an HTTP
      <code>429</code> response; the server cap is enforced when you register a new server. We
      reserve the right to modify tier features, allowances, or pricing with reasonable notice.
      Changes to paid tier pricing will not apply to a period you've already paid for.
    </p>

    <h2 id="payments-refunds-and-cancellation">6. Payments, Refunds, and Cancellation</h2>
    <p>Plus and Pro are billed as recurring monthly subscriptions. The following terms apply to all paid subscriptions.</p>
    <PaymentProvider />
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Upgrading.</strong> From the dashboard, go to Settings &gt; Billing and choose
        "Upgrade to Plus" or "Upgrade to Pro." This opens our payment provider's hosted checkout.
        Your new plan applies as soon as checkout completes.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Billing period and renewal.</strong> Paid plans are sold as monthly subscription
        periods and renew automatically at the end of each period until cancelled, charged to the
        payment method on file with our payment provider.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Cancelling.</strong> There is no in-app cancel. From Settings &gt; Billing, choose
        "Manage billing" to open the billing portal in a new tab, where you can cancel, switch
        plans, update your payment method, and download invoices — or cancel by emailing
        <a href="mailto:support@mcpwarp.io">support@mcpwarp.io</a>. When you cancel, your
        paid access <strong>continues until the end of the period you've already paid for</strong>,
        then your account returns to Free. We do not provide automatic partial refunds for the
        unused part of a billing period.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Downgrading.</strong> If you switch to a lower tier (or your subscription lapses
        to Free), existing servers are kept, but creating new servers is blocked while you're over
        your new plan's server cap (1 server on Free and Plus). On Free, the
        100-requests-per-month cap applies starting from your next request.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Failed payments and chargebacks.</strong> If a payment fails, is reversed, or is
        charged back, we may suspend or downgrade your paid access until the amount due is
        settled. If you believe a charge is wrong, contact
        <a href="mailto:support@mcpwarp.io">support@mcpwarp.io</a> first; we will normally resolve
        it faster than a dispute with your bank.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>14-day money-back guarantee.</strong> If you're not satisfied with your
        <strong>first</strong> payment for a paid subscription, you may request a full refund
        within <strong>14 days</strong> of that purchase by emailing
        <a href="mailto:support@mcpwarp.io">support@mcpwarp.io</a>. This guarantee applies to a
        first-time subscription purchase and does not apply to renewals.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Statutory rights unaffected.</strong> Nothing in this section limits any refund or
        cancellation rights you may have under applicable law. Consumers in the EU, EEA, and UK
        generally have a 14-day statutory right of withdrawal on digital purchases, in addition to
        the guarantee above.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>How refunds are issued.</strong> Refunds are processed by our payment provider
        under its own refund policy and returned to the original payment method where possible.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Changes to payment providers.</strong> We may add, replace, or stop using a
        payment provider. If a change requires you to re-authorize a subscription, we will notify
        active paid users by email. A change of provider does not shorten a period you've already
        paid for.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>See <a href="/docs/how-to/billing/">Manage your subscription</a> for a walkthrough of the billing flows described above.</p>

