      damage resulting from service interruptions, including lost connections or failed MCP
      requests.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Suspension and Termination</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>We may suspend or terminate your account if you violate these Terms, abuse the Service, or threaten its security or availability for other users.</li>
      <li>We will make reasonable efforts to notify you before or at the time of suspension, except where immediate action is necessary for security reasons.</li>
      <li>You may delete your account at any time by contacting <a href="mailto:support@mcpwarp.io">support@mcpwarp.io</a>.</li>
      <li>Upon termination, your tunnel URLs stop functioning immediately and all MCP client access is revoked.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>9. Data Processing</h2>
    <p>
      The tunnel relays MCP request and response bodies between your MCP client and your local
      server in real time. This traffic is <strong>not persisted</strong> by the Service — it is
      not written to disk, logged, or stored in a database. Your MCP servers, and the local
      targets they expose, run and execute entirely on your own machine; we never run your code
      for you. Connections between the CLI, the tunnel edge, and MCP clients use TLS encryption
      (terminated at Cloudflare). No system is perfectly secure, and transmitting data over the
      internet involves inherent risk.
    </p>

